# program-plan -- the ONE next move from "goal set" to "program written".
#
# WHAT THIS REPLACES (owner rehearsal 2026-09-26, gap list
# goal-to-program-handoff-gaps.md E1-E14 / H1-H6). The hand-off from the goal
# interview into the first workout program lived as prose in
# workout-program/SKILL.md (W1-W5) and reference/AGENT-CONSULT.md (G6/G7). The
# prose carried the rehearsal principles as rules the model was asked to keep:
# propose before asking, one decision per turn, never assume the user's
# circumstances, never leak internal vocabulary, never invent a number. It did
# not keep them: W4 put the whole week + substitutions + emphasis + a volume
# verdict into ONE confirm; sets and reps in the first program were composed by
# the model; place and days were open questions; days and times were asked in
# one breath; G7 re-confirmed what the kit wrap had already closed; "프로그램
# 카드" and below_floor-class terms had a path to the user.
#
# THE REPAIR IS STRUCTURAL, THE SAME WAY THE KIT'S `goal-interview --next` IS:
# this tool decides the next move and renders every sentence the user reads.
#   * `next` returns ONE move: {kind, stage, readback[], say, choices[],
#     answer}. The model speaks `readback` then `say` verbatim and records the
#     user's pick with `answer --stage <stage>`. There is no step counter and no
#     preview of later steps -- nothing to narrate.
#   * every number the user sees comes from a record, from the user's own
#     answer, or from a RULE TABLE in this file with its reason sentence
#     (RX_RULES / SPLIT_FAMILIES / WEEKDAY_SPREAD). Every lift has a rule
#     (core / hold / unclassified included), so no dose is ever asked --
#     and never a model-filled number. The compose payload REFUSES sets / reps /
#     weights outright (E-NUMBER-FROM-MODEL): the model names lifts, it does
#     not dose them.
#   * the safety check is a stage that runs BEFORE any number: before the
#     kit's first target proposal (the kit move loop has no safety move yet --
#     kit-side follow-up) and before the program's first dose.
#   * the kit's wrap IS the end of the goal part. The pack reads it, finishes
#     its own bookkeeping, and folds it into the program's FIRST decision
#     (the place, round 3) as ONE message: the goal card and one wrap line
#     are the readback, the place is the question. No second summary, no
#     second approval (old G7), no offer question of its own.
#   * round 2 (owner rehearsal 2026-09-26 13:27-14:32), held by `move()`:
#     every rendered move ends on the next decision (a question) -- a
#     confirmation is readback on the next move, never a message of its own;
#     no hand-gesture emoji, no code block, no backslash escape. A decision
#     move (`kind: decide`) is three options: a BOLD heading "N. name", its
#     one-line description on the next line, the week as a two-line calendar
#     (weekday header / one glyph per day, two spaces between cells, rest
#     U+318D, A/B fullwidth, 상/하, 전) as the ONLY quoted lines, then IMMEDIATELY (no blank
#     line, owner 15:12) pro / con as "•" bullets with text labels
#     ("• 장점: ..." / "• 단점: ...", owner 15:00 / 17:18: no traffic-light
#     markers, no +/-, no dash) -- so calendar and option buttons stay in ONE
#     message.
#   * a functional direction (a strand on a program-computed measure) adds
#     what every session carries beyond the lifts (CARE_ITEMS): emitted as
#     `care` data and written onto the card (program.yaml `care:`, through
#     program-init) -- in the consult they are the mat-prep and cooldown
#     slots of every session (round 3), not a block of their own -- so
#     session-open renders the same lines at every session start
#     (care_lines, one renderer for both surfaces).
#   * the kit's goal interview now asks the training age inside its 운동
#     slot and offers the care step on its health strand (card rehearsal
#     2026-09-26 17:03-17:18). Both answers land in config
#     (training_years_band / training_experience, goal_care) and are READ
#     here: the experience stage never asks what the kit stored, and care the
#     kit confirmed is plan data only -- the kit's card already shows it.
#   * user-facing copy is gated at import (_copy_gate): a template carrying an
#     internal term does not load.
#   * round 3, the PROGRAM CARD (owner rehearsal 2026-09-26 17:20-17:48). The
#     stage order is goal -> place -> daytime -> split -> focus -> compose
#     -> sessions -> done. The kit wrap folds into the FIRST program
#     question (the place, owner 17:40), not the split. Every program
#     message opens with the program card (program_card): a quote block of
#     the program's slots in flow order, unfilled "ㆍ", the slot asked now in
#     bold -- a filled line is the confirmation, never a message of its own.
#     Days and times are ONE slot, "운동일시" (17:44), with the optional
#     extra days filling the "보충" slot. The split menu is sized to the
#     regular day count; once picked, the next message explains ONCE that
#     sessions are a queue, not weekdays (17:29). The volume floor is held
#     INSIDE compose (17:38): the tool raises sets silently within the rule
#     range, and refuses a composed program it cannot bring to the floor, so
#     no volume question is ever asked. Compose also refuses muscle-group
#     back-and-forth inside a session (17:31) and activation core in the work
#     list (17:32: it lives in the mat-prep slot). All sessions are shown in
#     ONE message, each a plain blockquote with a set-derived title and
#     primary-muscle labels. Safety swaps and cardio are decided before
#     the preview; prep and cooldown each occupy one names-only line. The closing
#     message states the next session and asks nothing (17:48, the one
#     exception to "every message ends on a decision").
#   * the JOURNEY (owner-approved 2026-09-26 23:03, JOURNEY.md + AMENDMENTS
#     A1-A8): the order the user decides things is ONE tuple, `JOURNEY`;
#     `next` walks it and an answer out of order is refused (E-STAGE). A2:
